From d7294617134c86cb6419790bce810fbf2211750b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:18:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] target/mips: set up the MT ASE MVP registers from the
 CPU model

mvp_init() runs before the first CPU reset, which is what loads Config3
from the model, so ase_mt_available() was always false there and every
MT ASE CPU (34Kf, 1004Kc) got MVPConf0/MVPConf1 = 0: no TCs to address,
and MTTR/MFTR to TC 1+ were translated as NOPs.  Check the model's
Config3 instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012GbUcwR34gg9RgGTEtNN6J
---
 target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc b/target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc
index 1237f36..80aba3f 100644
--- a/target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc
+++ b/target/mips/cpu-defs.c.inc
@@ -1071,7 +1071,8 @@ static void mvp_init(CPUMIPSState *env)
 {
     env->mvp = g_malloc0(sizeof(CPUMIPSMVPContext));
 
-    if (!ase_mt_available(env)) {
+    /* (before the CPU reset, which loads Config3 from the model) */
+    if (!(env->cpu_model->CP0_Config3 & (1 << CP0C3_MT))) {
         return;
     }
 
